# Capacitor Android build output -- regenerable via `npx cap add android`
# (see capacitor.config.json), same convention as Winfinity's own
# capacitor-app/android/. `www/` is just a synced copy of the real web
# files (index.html/app.js/etc, already tracked at the repo root) that
# `npx cap sync` recreates -- not a second source of truth to track.
# EXCEPTION: these files hold real, hand-written native fixes (camera
# runtime-permission request + the AndroidManifest CAMERA permission it
# needs; the back-button JS bridge; and build.gradle's versionCode, which
# MUST increase with every real build or Android's installer forces an
# uninstall instead of an in-place update -- found the hard way after every
# single build this session shared the same hardcoded versionCode 1) that
# `npx cap add android` would NOT recreate -- losing any of them would
# silently reintroduce a real bug on any future from-scratch Android
# project regeneration. IMPORTANT: this is why the
# top-level pattern below is `android/*`, not a bare `android/` -- a bare
# directory pattern makes git skip descending into it entirely, for
# performance, so NO negation deeper inside it can ever take effect no
# matter how it's written (confirmed by testing: bare `android/` +
# `!android/app/` still reported the target file as ignored). `android/*`
# matches the same contents via glob instead, which still allows traversal.
# Verified end-to-end with `git check-ignore -v` and `git add -n` after
# writing this -- don't trust gitignore negation blindly, it's easy to get
# subtly wrong in a way that *looks* right.
android/*
# Also hand-written (added for the Jitsi Meet Android SDK integration --
# Class Sessions' native video call screen): the root build.gradle's
# jitsi-maven-repository Maven repo entry, and variables.gradle's
# minSdkVersion bump to 26 (jitsi-meet-sdk's own manifest requires it).
# Neither of these is regenerated by `npx cap add android` -- losing them
# silently breaks the Jitsi dependency resolution/manifest merge again with
# no clue why, same risk class as the exceptions above.
!android/build.gradle
!android/variables.gradle
!android/app/
android/app/*
!android/app/build.gradle
!android/app/src/
android/app/src/*
!android/app/src/main/
android/app/src/main/*
!android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
!android/app/src/main/java/
android/app/src/main/java/*
!android/app/src/main/java/io/
android/app/src/main/java/io/*
!android/app/src/main/java/io/github/
android/app/src/main/java/io/github/*
!android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/
android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/*
!android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/squizit/
android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/squizit/*
!android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/squizit/MainActivity.java
!android/app/src/main/java/io/github/winfos/squizit/SplashActivity.java
# Also hand-written: the native splash screen's theme, layout, and glow
# drawable (see SplashActivity.java) -- everything else under res/ is
# regenerable default Capacitor icon/splash-image output.
!android/app/src/main/res/
android/app/src/main/res/*
!android/app/src/main/res/values/
android/app/src/main/res/values/*
!android/app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml
!android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
!android/app/src/main/res/layout/
android/app/src/main/res/layout/*
!android/app/src/main/res/layout/activity_splash.xml
!android/app/src/main/res/drawable/
android/app/src/main/res/drawable/*
!android/app/src/main/res/drawable/splash_glow.xml
!android/app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/
android/app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/*
!android/app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/splash_icon.png
www/

